asset:        1100-quickwins.aep
title:        After Effects project: HDR Highlight Compression, Echo, Linear Wipe, Offset and Color Stabilizer, one composition per variant (defaults, every parameter set, minimum and maximum, popup items, keyframes, expression)
author:       vangel76 (contributor)
source:       original work; group 1100-quickwins of tools/aep/importer-samples/jsx/g1-quickwins.jsx (EffectCraft issue 3110); generation notes docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md
license:      MIT OR Apache-2.0
license-file: ../LICENSE-MIT, ../LICENSE-APACHE
added:        2026-11-05 by @vangel76
notes:        Generated from scratch by the contributor with Adobe After Effects 2026 (26.2.1x2) on Windows 11 as their own test data for the effectcraft-aep tests; it holds only synthetic project structure, no third-party footage, template or personal data, and no Adobe sample project, preset or asset was used. Compositions are named like the renders (hdr-, echo-, linwipe-, offset-, colstab-; 75 variants, aep/readbacks/1100-quickwins.json lists what was set and what After Effects read back). Sources: the SRC test card built from solids by the script (no footage) and aep/media/crypto-320x180.exr. 32 bpc, working space None. Saved-file cleanup, in this order: (1) the footage link of the EXR names a contributor-made file that is not included here (aep/media/ holds the same EXR); its stored path and the host name were replaced by neutral ones of the same length (tools/aep/scrub.py); the XMP packet after the project container was replaced by the packet of empty.aep; (2) tools/aep/scrub-uninit.py zeroed what After Effects had written from uninitialised memory (scrub-uninit.py found nothing to change in this file; details in docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md); (3) the embedded ICC profile of the working space was replaced by a description-only stub (tools/aep/stubicc.rs: 128-byte header, one `desc` tag, no colour data), which keeps the profile name for metadata tests and is not a colour-transform oracle. Final bytes checked with tools/aep/inspect-embedded.py (raw, base64 and hex, with the local user, host and folder names as --forbid): CLEAN. A chunk-by-chunk comparison with the saved file and an import of both files with the importer show that only those records changed (docs/aep/2026-11-05-importer-samples.md).
